{# version: 1 #}
{#- Evaluation-only prompt (app/eval/ablate.py, ablations A2 and A3). The rules and field
    definitions are copied from extract_front / extract_experiments so that only the
    granularity (which text, which fields per call) and the quote requirement change. -#}
You extract structured information from a research paper. Use only the text below
(sections, tables and appendix excerpts). Every paragraph or table starts with an id in
brackets.

Rules for every item:
{% if quotes -%}
- "value": a short statement in your own words.
- "quote": ONE sentence (or one table caption/row) copied character-for-character from the
  text that states the item.
- "chunk_id": the id in brackets of the paragraph or table the quote comes from.
{% else -%}
- "value": a short statement in your own words.
{% endif -%}
- "confidence": 0 to 1.
- If the text does not state something, return an empty list for it. Never invent items.
- Do not compute or convert numbers; copy values exactly as written (e.g. "3e-4", "50k").

Fields:
{% for f in fields -%}
{% if f == "task" -%}
- task: the task(s) studied, e.g. "machine translation", "image classification".
{% elif f == "datasets" -%}
- datasets: every dataset used. name as written; split(s) used; size as stated; public:
  "yes" if it is a public benchmark, "no" if private/internal, otherwise "unknown".
{% elif f == "baselines" -%}
- baselines: methods the paper compares against.
{% elif f == "metrics" -%}
- metrics: evaluation metrics (e.g. BLEU, top-1 accuracy, F1).
{% elif f == "hyperparameters" -%}
- hyperparameters: name, value_raw exactly as written, scope (e.g. "pre-training",
  "fine-tuning") or empty. Include optimizer, learning rate, batch size, epochs/steps,
  dropout, warmup, model sizes.
{% elif f == "compute" -%}
- compute: hardware, number of devices, training time or GPU hours.
{% endif -%}
{% endfor %}
{% if hints %}
Hints found by pattern matching (they may be wrong or incomplete; check them against the text):
{% for h in hints -%}
- {{ h.kind }} in [{{ h.block_id }}]: {{ h.sentence }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
Text:
{{ text }}
